tory in Liaoning, Hebei, Shaanxi, Shandong and Henan'; the Jin's loss is Cliopatria's, not a page's.","cp":"later-yan","cpn":"Later Yan","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Later_Yan","c":1},{"y":394,"t":"loss","x":"394: Shandong goes to Later Yan.","cp":"later-yan","cpn":"Later Yan","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Later_Yan","c":2},{"y":403,"t":"rename","x":"403: Huan Xuan usurps the throne.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":404,"t":"rename","x":"404: Liu Yu overthrows Huan Xuan and restores the Jin ('after leading a rebellion in 404 to overthrow Huan Xuan').","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":405,"t":"loss","x":"405: Qiao Zong's Western Shu secedes.","cp":"western-shu","cpn":"Western Shu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":409,"t":"contest_start","x":"409: Liu Yu marches on the Southern Yan.","cp":"southern-yan","cpn":"Southern Yan","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteen_Kingdoms","c":3},{"y":410,"t":"gain","x":"410: Shandong returns.","cp":"southern-yan","cpn":"Southern Yan","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":410,"t":"contest_end","x":"410: Southern Yan ends.","cp":"southern-yan","cpn":"Southern Yan","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":412,"t":"contest_start","x":"Late 412: Liu Yu sends Zhu Lingshi against the Western Shu.","cp":"western-shu","cpn":"Western Shu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":2},{"y":413,"t":"gain","x":"413: Western Shu is taken back.","cp":"western-shu","cpn":"Western Shu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":413,"t":"contest_end","x":"413: Chengdu falls and Western Shu ends, 'capturing Chengdu in 413 and annexing Western Shu back into Jin'.","cp":"western-shu","cpn":"Western Shu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":416,"t":"contest_start","x":"416: Liu Yu's northern expedition.","cp":"later-qin","cpn":"Later Qin","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":417,"t":"gain","x":"417: Chang'an falls.","cp":"later-qin","cpn":"Later Qin","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":417,"t":"contest_end","x":"417: Later Qin ends.","cp":"later-qin","cpn":"Later Qin","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3},{"y":418,"t":"contest_start","x":"418: Xia strikes at Chang'an.","cp":"xia","cpn":"Xia (Helian Xia)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":2},{"y":418,"t":"loss","x":"418: Xia takes Guanzhong.","cp":"xia","cpn":"Xia (Helian Xia)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteen_Kingdoms","c":3},{"y":418,"t":"contest_end","x":"418: Liu Yu abandons his plans against Xia; the frontier stays.","cp":"xia","cpn":"Xia (Helian Xia)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteen_Kingdoms","c":2},{"y":420,"t":"dissolve","x":"420: Liu Yu ends the Jin.","m":7,"cp":"liu-song-dynasty","cpn":"Liu Song dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Conquest of Wu by Jin","from":279,"to":280,"outcome":"Jin wins: Jiangling 3 April, Wuchang mid-April, Jiao and Guang surrender in April, Sun Hao surrenders 1 May 280.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conquest_of_Wu_by_Jin"},{"name":"War of the Eight Princes","from":291,"to":306,"outcome":"'A series of civil wars' that 'weakened it considerably'; no frontier changed, but Cheng-Han and Han-Zhao rose in 304.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jin_dynasty_(266%E2%80%93420)"},{"name":"Rise of Cheng-Han in Yi Province","from":301,"to":314,"outcome":"Li Te's rebellion from 301, Li Xiong king of Chengdu in 304 and emperor in 306, Luo Shang dead in 310, Hanzhong ceded in 314.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheng-Han"},{"name":"Han-Zhao conquest of the Jin heartland (Disaster of Yongjia)","from":304,"to":316,"outcome":"Luoyang falls and Emperor Huai is captured in 311; Chang'an falls and Emperor Min is captured in 316, ending the Western Jin.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han-Zhao"},{"name":"Goguryeo conquest of Lelang and Daifang","from":313,"to":314,"outcome":"Goguryeo annexes Lelang in 313 and attacks Daifang in 314.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lelang_Commandery"},{"name":"Huan Wen's conquest of Cheng-Han","from":346,"to":347,"outcome":"Li Shi surrenders at Chengdu in 347.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huan_Wen"},{"name":"Linyi (Lâm Ấp) attacks on Jin Jiaozhou","from":347,"to":413,"outcome":"'In 347, king Fan Wen (范文) attacked Jin-controlled Jiaozhou with 40–50,000 troops'; in 399 Bhadravarman 'tried to seize the coast of Jiaozhou and Rinan'; in 413 he 'attacked Jiao again, but was defeated, captured and beheaded by the Governor of Jiaozhou, Du…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A2m_%E1%BA%A4p"},{"name":"Huan Wen's northern expeditions","from":354,"to":369,"outcome":"Chang'an not reached in 354; Luoyang held 356-365; the 369 expedition ends in defeat at Fangtou.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huan_Wen"},{"name":"Former Qin-Jin war and the Battle of Fei River","from":373,"to":383,"outcome":"Former Qin takes Sichuan (373) and Xiangyang (379); the Jin wins at the Fei River (November 383) and recovers territories south of the Yellow River.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Fei_River"},{"name":"Sun En's rebellion","from":399,"to":411,"outcome":"Sun En 'captured Kuaiji' and fled to Zhoushan Island; Liu Yu beat him at Haiyan in winter 401 and he died in battle in 401 (Emperor Wu page) or 'April or May 402' (Sun En page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_En"},{"name":"Huan Xuan's usurpation","from":403,"to":404,"outcome":"Huan Xuan takes the throne in winter 403 and is overthrown by Liu Yu in 404.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song"},{"name":"Liu Yu's conquest of Western Shu","from":407,"to":413,"outcome":"Liu Jingxuan's attack of 407 'stalled in 408'; Zhu Lingshi, commissioned in late 412, took Chengdu in 413 and annexed Western Shu back into Jin.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song"},{"name":"Liu Yu's conquest of the Southern Yan","from":409,"to":410,"outcome":"Guanggu falls in spring 410; Shandong recovered.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song"},{"name":"Liu Yu's northern expedition against Later Qin","from":416,"to":418,"outcome":"Luoyang falls in winter 416, Chang'an in spring 417; Xia seizes Guanzhong in 418 and Jin keeps the Luoyang region.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song"}],"certainty":[{"from":266,"to":420,"level":"soft","note":"No page opened gives a boundary line."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jin_dynasty_(266%E2%80%93420)","title":"Jin dynasty (266-420)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Jin_dynasty","title":"Western Jin dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conquest_of_Wu_by_Jin","title":"Conquest of Wu by Jin"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han-Zhao","title":"Han-Zhao"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheng-Han","title":"Cheng-Han"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Former_Liang","title":"Former Liang"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lelang_Commandery","title":"Lelang Commandery"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huan_Wen","title":"Huan Wen"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Fei_River","title":"Battle of Fei River"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Wu_of_Liu_Song","title":"Emperor Wu of Liu Song"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixteen_Kingdoms","title":"Sixteen Kingdoms"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chief_Official_of_the_Western_Regions","title":"Chief Official of the Western Regions"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protectorate_of_the_Western_Regions","title":"Protectorate of the Western Regions"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cao_Wei","title":"Cao Wei"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Shu","title":"Western Shu"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Huai_of_Jin","title":"Emperor Huai of Jin"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Later_Yan","title":"Later Yan"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daifang_Commandery","title":"Daifang Commandery"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murong_Hui","title":"Murong Hui"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_En","title":"Sun En"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A2m_%E1%BA%A4p","title":"Lâm Ấp"}]}